l fimbriations 1/32 inch.\n\n===Symbolism:===\n\n* The functions of the organization are indicated by the double-handed sword, symbolic of protection, over the '''Washington Monument''', representing the area concerned. The blue represents the '''Navy''' and the '''Infantry'''; the scarlet the '''Field Artillery''', '''Coast Artillery''' and '''Engineers''', and the green and gold the '''Military Police'''.\n\n===Background:===\n\n* The shoulder sleeve insignia was originally approved for '''Military District of Washington''' on [[September 26]], [[1942]] and redesignated for '''US Army Military District of Washington''' on [[July 21]], [[1971]].\n\n== {{int:license-header}} ==\n{{PD-USGov-Military-Army-USAIOH}} - US Army Institute Of Heraldry\n\n[[Category:Shoulder Sleeve Insignia of the United States Army (SSI)]]\n[[Category:Media missing infobox template]]\n[[Category:Combat service identification badges of the United States Army]]"}}}]},{"pageid":2141145,"ns":6,"title":"File:12th Army Group.svg","imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"timestamp":"2007-05-22T12:54:11Z","user":"Beringar","size":910,"width":160,"height":213,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/12th_Army_Group.svg/500px-12th_Army_Group.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":360,"thumbheight":480,"responsiveUrls":{"2":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/12th_Army_Group.svg/960px-12th_Army_Group.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail"},"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/12th_Army_Group.svg/500px-12th_Army_Group.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":360,"height":480,"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/12th_Army_Group.svg/960px-12th_Army_Group.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimed